<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dengzhou</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Penglai</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dengzhou was a prefecture and port on the northern coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shandong">Shandong</a> peninsula in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, at modern Penglai, facing the Bohai Strait. It was a main harbour for sea traffic between China, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a>. In 732 a Balhae fleet under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jang-mun-hyu">Jang Mun-hyu</a> raided it and killed the prefect, and in later centuries it was an important naval base.</p></div>
